    "Scouting Notes": "Starter or Long Relief\n High 80's to low 90's fastball, but has some Freddy Peralta qualities to the pitch. Seems to get on top of hitters much faster than the radar gun would tell you.\n Gets good extension and hides the ball well with a long arm action and throwing from a high slot, which helps the fastball play up.\n Appears to generate some cut on the fastball, unsure if it's on purpose or just his release. Seems to help him miss some barrels. Might be worth trying to make it a separate pitch, if it isn't already.\n Slider is a solid secondary, curve not far behind.\n Have not seen much in the way of a changeup, but the few times I've seen it, I'm not sure it's even worth tossing in. Not a very good pitch presently.\n Command is solid, but could use improvement, as the stuff itself is more in the average range. Walks spiked at High A.\n Numbers in Carolina were good, despite a higher ERA. He struck a lot of people out and limited walks. He earned the higher ERA in High A though.\n He's interesting, due to the way the fastball plays. He's not super young anymore though at 22. Needs to have a good start to next year.\n Somewhat surprised by him being released.",
